          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %strong exact category
            (in the sense of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Barr71"} Barr 1971
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            in which every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            (that is, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            is
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective
            = succeed "." do
              %strong effective regular categories
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              See
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/familial+regularity+and+exactness"} familial regularity and exactness
              for a generalization of exactness and its relationship to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensivity
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\hookrightarrow X\times X
              is a congruence which is the kernel pair of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X \to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = m \circ p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image+factorization"} image factorization
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient
            %p
              However, not
              %em every
              parallel pair of morphisms need have a coequalizer, and there are also regular categories having all coequalizers which are not exact.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
              of an exact category is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"}> 2-sheaf
              ) for its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\rightrightarrows A
              is a kernel pair, then so is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*R \rightrightarrows B
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B\to A
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                is an exact category.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, so is every
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+colimit"} van Kampen
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
                is exact. See at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+colimit"} van Kampen colimit
                for a proof.
            %li
              %p
                Any category which is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monadic
                over a power of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                is exact. A proof may be found
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+in+categories+of+algebras#exact"} here
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                is exact. In fact an abelian category is precisely an exact
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is exact and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod(T, C)
                of
                = succeed "-models" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is also exact. See Theorem 5.11 of Barr’s
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Barr"} Exact Categories
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice"} slice
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-slice"} co-slice
                of an exact category is also exact. (Source:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.springer.com/us/book/9781402019616"} Borceux and Bourn
            %li
              %p
                One can construct, for any regular category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                by adjoining formal quotient objects for congruences. One way to define
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                is as the (locally discrete)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                whose objects are congruences in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and whose morphisms are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is already exact, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                is equivalent to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+and+exact+completions"} regular and exact completions
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, one can construct the “free” exact category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                on any category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with finite limits, or even with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} weak finite limits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                for a category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with weak finite limits are exactly those which have
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} enough (regular) projectives
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (Carboni-Vitale 1998). See
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+and+exact+completions"} regular and exact completions
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
